Based on my examination of the index.html template file, here's a detailed analysis of the current CSS styling and layout structure:

## 1. Top Summary Box Layout Analysis

**Current Layout (lines 90-95):**
```css
.summary-stats {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 30px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}
```

**Issue:** The current layout uses horizontal flexbox with `flex-wrap: wrap`, which means:
- On wide screens, items try to fit horizontally first, then wrap
- This creates inconsistent vertical stacking behavior
- The layout doesn't stack vertically by default like it should

**Individual Summary Stat Styling (lines 97-110):**
```css
.summary-stat {
    text-align: center;
}

.summary-stat .number {
    font-size: 1.5em;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #2196f3;
}

.summary-stat .label {
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.9em;
}
```

## 2. Text Wrapping/Overflow Issues

**Project Name Styling (lines 48-61):**
```css
.project-name {
    font-size: 1.2em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.project-name a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #2196f3;
}
```

**Issues Found:**
- No `word-break` or `overflow-wrap` properties are defined
- Long project/directory names could overflow containers
- No text truncation or ellipsis handling for extremely long names

**Project Stats Layout (lines 63-75):**
```css
.project-stats {
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
}
```

## 3. Time Display Format Analysis

**Current Time Display Implementation:**
- Line 140: `<div class='label'>Last: {{ summary.formatted_latest_interaction }}</div>`
- Line 155: `<div class='stat'>🕒 {{ project.formatted_date }}</div>`
- Line 160: `<div class='stat'>🕐 Last: {{ project.formatted_last_interaction }}</div>`

**Current Time Display Logic:**
The template relies on backend-formatted time strings:
- `summary.formatted_latest_interaction`
- `project.formatted_date`
- `project.formatted_last_interaction`

**Issues:**
- No time interval/relative time display (e.g., "2 hours ago")
- Time formatting is handled server-side, limiting client-side time updates
- No indication of how old the interactions are

## Required Modifications

### 1. Fix Top Summary Box Layout
Change `.summary-stats` from horizontal to vertical stacking:
```css
.summary-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;  /* Force vertical stacking */
    align-items: center;     /* Center items horizontally */
    gap: 15px;              /* Reduce gap for vertical layout */
}
```

### 2. Fix Text Overflow Issues
Add proper text wrapping to `.project-name`:
```css
.project-name {
    font-size: 1.2em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    word-wrap: break-word;      /* Break long words */
    overflow-wrap: break-word;   /* Modern browsers */
    hyphens: auto;              /* Add hyphens for better readability */
}
```

### 3. Time Display Enhancements
The template would need JavaScript to add time intervals, or the backend formatting logic needs to be enhanced to include relative time information.

**Current CSS Selectors Needing Modification:**
- `.summary-stats` (line 90) - Layout direction
- `.project-name` (line 48) - Text overflow handling
- Time display elements don't need CSS changes, but backend formatting needs enhancement

The current layout structure is clean and well-organized, but these specific issues need addressing for better responsive behavior and text handling.

